// CROWN — the gate propagates OUTWARD: `outer(k) = run(k)` copies run's
// gated cell and binds the copy to k's row, so k's cell carries `!E` in
// outer's published scheme (`∀r. (E ∉ r) ⇒ …`, Gaster–Jones `lacks`), and
// main's callback refuses at outer's argument edge. Accepted by boot
// 2974547b (exit 7). Expect E_EffectMismatch.
effect E { op() -> Int }
handler h { op() => resume(7) }
fn run(f) with !E = f()
fn outer(k) = run(k)
fn main() = (outer(() => op())) ~> h
